  "worksAsStation": false,
  "description": "Partners share one puck and start close together. The carrier makes a short pass (about 5 feet), then skates ahead into open ice. The partner makes a long pass (about 15–20 feet) and follows it, so the two are close again for the next short pass. They work up the ice this way, trading jobs, and the next pair goes at the second pylon.",
  "steps": [
    "Short pass to your partner.",
    "Skate ahead into open ice.",
    "Partner makes a long pass to you.",
    "Partner follows the pass so you’re close again. Repeat up the ice.",
    "Next pair goes when the first reaches the second pylon."
  ],
